4. Mocked the generateNonce function that was causing the error
5. Simplified the provider structure to reduce complexity
6. Kept the error boundary for safety

The main changes focus on:
- Mocking the crypto module functionality
- Providing a simple implementation of randomBytes
- Making the mock available globally
- Ensuring the generateNonce function is available

This should resolve the crypto module error while still allowing the component to render. If you encounter any other specific errors after this change, please let me know and we can address them.

